Z||000005||2FAST4U||12-29-1999||11:39 PM||||Tom;<BR>If you wern't there you just can't believe how good it was.<BR>That picture brings back so many great memories.<BR>I started my journey into cars and hot rodding in a shop much like the one in the picture. Except our shop wasn't quite that big. You could get 2 cars in ours if you pushed the first car to the side with a floor jack. We ran a normal repiar shop during the day and built our hot rods at night with the money we made during the day.<BR>True, there were no Fieros then but there were 56 Fords with supercharged 292s taken from T-birds, and 57 small block Chevies, plus great cars built from scratch like the ones you see in the picture. Not only that but we had cars to dream about just like today. Today we dream about Lambos and Porches (sp) abd back then we dreamed (drempt?) about Fairlane Thunderbolts and Shelby Cobras.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-29-1999||11:53 PM||||Phil--Just a thought, but that pic took forever to load.  Next time try converting your pic to JPEG (with something like ACDSee) before you post it.  It will be compressed and might load faster.  I noticed that the pic is a GIF.  That's what my scanner scans pics as, too.  ACDSee is a free "trial" download.  I've used up my trial period, so I need to download it again, but it's really a cool thing to have on your computer.  I was told about it from another forum member.||||reg||1
