Z||000017||Phil||12-30-1999||08:55 AM||||Actually the car started life as a Model A four door pheaton(sp) front and rear doors were cut out and the rest welded back together and dropped over the rails. '32 grill shell. .127 over pistons and Merc crank(272 cu in), 3 Stromberg 97s, Isky cam,  Offy heads(with chrome acorn nuts-natch)and Mallory rev-pole ign. 411 rear. The beast would actually pull the front wheels. Our total investment was about $300. People were just about giving flathead parts away back then.||||reg||1
Z||000018||ChadMan||12-30-1999||09:53 AM||||Great photo, Phil.  I grew up hearing my dad reminisce about his hot rod (54 Ford w/T-bird V8 & 3 deuces) and complaining because the hottest Mustang you could buy was a turbo 4-banger.  Thank God performance cars came back!<P>I bought a fantastic book called The American Hot Rod by Dean Batchelor, which chronicles the birth of the hot-rodding movement in So.Cal., with an emphasis on T- and A-model Fords.  Great chapter on flatheads.  Amazon has it for $21.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Richard Parnell||12-30-1999||03:04 PM||||Cooter, don't throw that flathead v8 out.  Those are some of the best engines ever made.  Also you can convert them to hemis which is really cool.  One of the greatest cars I ever owned was a 49 Ford with a 52 or 53 flathead Mercury engine bored and stroked with 3 two barrels. I should never have sold that car.  I saw thw car years later still running like a top, a noisy one because of the solid lifters.  What a car--but I still love my Fiero even tho it would never make it as a makout car at the drive-in.  Does anyone remember drive-ins?||||reg||1
Z||000020||Formula||12-30-1999||07:05 PM||||The Fieros not a make out car......<BR>D.A.M.N. <P>Did I break the fiero law?<P>The Fiero to me is what the 42 Fords were to you guys.<P>Except my generation has economy rice burners to play with, so next time you see a souped up honda civic just think to yourself "He needs a time capsule" LMAO||||reg||1
Z||000021||Phil||12-30-1999||10:28 PM||||There were no 42 Fords for sale to the public||||reg||1
